   (MIT License).

Third-party copyright and license notices that remain in specific files,
such as src/algorithm/scrypt.h (Colin Percival), must be preserved in
redistribution. src/algorithm/sha256_neon.c credits public-domain work by
Jeffrey Walton (noloader/SHA-Intrinsics).

The RandomX hashing library (third_party/RandomX/, BSD 3-Clause,
Copyright (c) tevador and The Monero Project) is vendored unmodified;
its LICENSE file must be preserved in redistribution (text also
retained at LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause-RandomX.txt so binary packages
that ship the LICENSES/ directory satisfy this).

The yespower proof-of-work library (third_party/yespower/, BSD 2-Clause,
Copyright 2009 Colin Percival, Copyright 2013-2018 Alexander Peslyak) is
vendored unmodified from https://github.com/openwall/yespower; its LICENSE
file must be preserved in redistribution (text also retained at
LICENSES/BSD-2-Clause-yespower.txt). It is used by src/algorithm/civiclight.cpp
(the CIVIC/CivicNet "civiclight" algorithm), which is this project's own
clean-room implementation of that algorithm's combination logic, written
from a plain-language description rather than derived from CivicLight's
own source (their repos carry no license, so their code isn't cleared for
reuse here).
